-- title:
--   Width divisibility is unchanged by the shift k ↦ k+p+1
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$, let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $N$ be a positive natural number with $(N : K) \neq 0$, i.e. $p \nmid N$. Let $x$ be a place of the modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ K\ N$ over $K$, that is, a valuation subring of the field of formal Laurent series over $K$ restricted to the $K$-subfield generated by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{jqModC}\ K$ and $\mathrm{jqNModC}\ K\ N$, the subring being proper, containing the image of $K$ and a principal ideal ring. Assume $x$ lies in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ p\ N\ K$, i.e. $x$ is rational, is an affine geometric place in the sense of `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and the residue value $a_0 = x.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ K\ N)$ of the generator $j$ belongs to $\mathrm{ssJSet}\ p\ K$. Let $k$ be an integer with $2 \le k$ and $2 \mid k$. Then the width $\mathrm{placeWidth}\ N\ x$, defined as the quotient of $\mathrm{jWidth}(a_0)$ (equal to $3$ if $a_0 = 0$, to $2$ if $a_0 = 1728$, and to $1$ otherwise) by the ramification index $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\ N\ x$, divides $k/2$ if and only if it divides $(k + (p+1))/2$, both quotients being taken in $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   This is the index-set invariance underlying the weight ladder $k \mapsto k + p + 1$ for supersingular spaces: the divisibility condition singling out, at a supersingular place, the weights compatible with the local width is unaffected by adding $p+1$. It is used in the construction of the Hecke action on supersingular carriers, [`ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.exists_linearEquiv_ssCarrier_forall_ssHeckeFun_eq_smul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.exists_linearEquiv_ssCarrier_forall_ssHeckeFun_eq_smul).
